#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Obtain samples from an ansatz {#obtain-samples-from-an-ansatz}"
msgstr "Dapatkan sampel dari ansatz {#obtain-samples-from-an-ansatz}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once the molecule information has been loaded in, you should specify an "
"ansatz circuit and optimize it for execution. This involves considering any "
"symmetries of your problem, the choice of ansatz, and optimize it to run on "
"quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setelah informasi molekul dimuat, kamu perlu menentukan circuit ansatz dan "
"mengoptimalkannya untuk eksekusi. Ini melibatkan pertimbangan simetri "
"masalahmu, pemilihan ansatz, dan optimasi untuk dijalankan di hardware "
"kuantum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, these choices are problem specific and out of scope for this guide."
" Instead, to demonstrate the SQD workflow, we will generate a random set of "
"counts for the configuration recovery loop to post-process. This simulates "
"the measurement data of a 32-qubit circuit sampled with 10,000 shots. After "
"the count data has been generated, the `recover_configurations()` method "
"requires that you convert the count data into a matrix of the bitstrings "
"measured at each shot, as well as an array of probabilities for each state "
"that was measured.\n"
msgstr ""
"Namun, pilihan-pilihan ini bersifat spesifik terhadap masalah dan berada di "
"luar cakupan panduan ini. Sebagai gantinya, untuk mendemonstrasikan alur "
"kerja SQD, kita akan menghasilkan sekumpulan counts acak yang akan diproses "
"oleh configuration recovery loop. Ini mensimulasikan data pengukuran dari "
"circuit 32-Qubit yang disampling dengan 10.000 shot. Setelah data count "
"dihasilkan, metode `recover_configurations()` mengharuskan kamu mengkonversi"
" data count menjadi matriks bitstring yang diukur di setiap shot, serta "
"array probabilitas untuk setiap state yang diukur.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"The artificial generation of samples is only used as a means to demonstrate the tooling of `qiskit-addon-sqd`. The package is meant to be used as part of a larger workflow wherein an ansatz or other circuit is defined, optimized, and executed using the Sampler primitive. The code cell below contains commented-out code demonstrating what a typical workflow might look like given a circuit ansatz transpiled to an ISA circuit.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Pembuatan sampel secara artifisial ini hanya digunakan sebagai cara untuk mendemonstrasikan alat-alat `qiskit-addon-sqd`. Paket ini dimaksudkan untuk digunakan sebagai bagian dari alur kerja yang lebih besar, di mana sebuah ansatz atau circuit lain didefinisikan, dioptimalkan, dan dieksekusi menggunakan primitif Sampler. Sel kode di bawah ini berisi kode yang dikomentari yang mendemonstrasikan seperti apa alur kerja tipikal dengan circuit ansatz yang telah ditranspilasi ke ISA circuit.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run configuration recovery loop {#run-configuration-recovery-loop}"
msgstr ""
"Jalankan configuration recovery loop {#run-configuration-recovery-loop}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The measurement samples can then be refined by repeating the configuration "
"recovery and diagonalizing sets of subsamples to approximate the ground "
"state until convergence.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sampel pengukuran kemudian dapat disempurnakan dengan mengulang "
"configuration recovery dan mendiagonalisasi sekumpulan subsampel untuk "
"memperkirakan ground state hingga konvergen.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "First, specify the following options:\n"
msgstr "Pertama, tentukan opsi-opsi berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ITERATIONS`: The number of self-consistent configuration recovery "
"iterations\n"
msgstr ""
"`ITERATIONS`: Jumlah iterasi configuration recovery yang self-consistent\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`NUM_BATCHES`: The number of sets of subsamples to diagonalize\n"
msgstr "`NUM_BATCHES`: Jumlah set subsampel yang akan didiagonalisasi\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`SAMPLES_PER_BATCH`: The number of samples to include in each batch\n"
msgstr "`SAMPLES_PER_BATCH`: Jumlah sampel yang disertakan di setiap batch\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`MAX_DAVIDSON_CYCLES`: The number of iterations for the eigenstate solver\n"
msgstr "`MAX_DAVIDSON_CYCLES`: Jumlah iterasi untuk eigenstate solver\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As an optional step, you can define a callback function to log the details "
"for each configuration recovery iteration.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai langkah opsional, kamu bisa mendefinisikan fungsi callback untuk "
"mencatat detail setiap iterasi configuration recovery.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, run the configuration recovery loop. Each loop consists of three "
"steps:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang, jalankan configuration recovery loop. Setiap loop terdiri dari "
"tiga langkah:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use the `recover_configurations()` function to obtain a refined bitstring "
"matrix and probability array based on the average orbital occupancy.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gunakan fungsi `recover_configurations()` untuk mendapatkan matriks "
"bitstring yang telah diperhalus dan array probabilitas berdasarkan rata-rata"
" orbital occupancy.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use the `postselect_and_subsample()` to collect batches of subsamples to "
"diagonalize over.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gunakan `postselect_and_subsample()` untuk mengumpulkan batch subsampel yang"
" akan didiagonalisasi.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then use the batches of subsamples as arguments to the `solve_fermion()` "
"function to obtain an approximation of the ground state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kemudian gunakan batch subsampel sebagai argumen ke fungsi `solve_fermion()`"
" untuk memperoleh perkiraan ground state.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is important to note how to address the first iteration of the "
"configuration recovery loop. Since the average orbital occupancy is not yet "
"available, only the `postselect_and_subsample()` function is called. This "
"removes any non-physical samples (samples with incorrect Hamming weight) "
"before running the eigenstate solver, `solve_fermion()`. Afterward, the "
"average orbital occupation is calculated across all batches and used as "
"input to the `recover_configurations()` method, which flips individual bits "
"probabilistically based on this average. See Section **II-A** of the "
"supplementary information in the [SQD "
"paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.05068) for more information.\n"
msgstr ""
"Penting untuk diperhatikan bagaimana cara menangani iterasi pertama dari "
"configuration recovery loop. Karena rata-rata orbital occupancy belum "
"tersedia, hanya fungsi `postselect_and_subsample()` yang dipanggil. Ini "
"menghilangkan sampel yang tidak fisik (sampel dengan Hamming weight yang "
"salah) sebelum menjalankan eigenstate solver, `solve_fermion()`. Setelah "
"itu, rata-rata orbital occupation dihitung di semua batch dan digunakan "
"sebagai input ke metode `recover_configurations()`, yang membalik bit "
"individual secara probabilistik berdasarkan rata-rata ini. Lihat Bagian "
"**II-A** dari informasi tambahan di [makalah "
"SQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.05068) untuk informasi lebih lanjut.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Visualize the results {#visualize-the-results}"
msgstr "Visualisasikan hasilnya {#visualize-the-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Lastly, the results can be visualized by examining the approximated energy "
"and average orbital occupancy at each iteration of the configuration "
"recovery loop. The first plot shows that after a few iterations, the ground "
"state energy is estimated to within approximately `27 mH` (chemical accuracy"
" is typically accepted to be `1 kcal/mol` $\\approx$ `1.6 mH`). Recall that "
"this demonstration used pure noise, and that the ability to approximate the "
"energy to this degree comes from prior knowledge about the molecule and its "
"electronic structure.\n"
msgstr ""
"Terakhir, hasil dapat divisualisasikan dengan memeriksa energi yang "
"diperkirakan dan rata-rata orbital occupancy di setiap iterasi dari "
"configuration recovery loop. Plot pertama menunjukkan bahwa setelah beberapa"
" iterasi, energi ground state diperkirakan dalam kisaran sekitar `27 mH` "
"(akurasi kimia umumnya diterima sebagai `1 kcal/mol` $\\approx$ `1.6 mH`). "
"Ingat bahwa demonstrasi ini menggunakan noise murni, dan kemampuan untuk "
"memperkirakan energi hingga tingkat ini berasal dari pengetahuan awal "
"tentang molekul dan struktur elektroniknya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The second plot shows the average occupancy of each spatial orbital after "
"the final iteration. Notice that both the spin-up and spin-down electrons "
"occupy the first five orbitals with high probability in the solutions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Plot kedua menunjukkan rata-rata occupancy setiap orbital spasial setelah "
"iterasi terakhir. Perhatikan bahwa baik elektron spin-up maupun spin-down "
"menempati lima orbital pertama dengan probabilitas tinggi dalam solusinya.\n"

